Time Complexity:
O(n²)

Space Complexity:
O(1)

Approach:
1. Traverse each index as the starting point of a subarray
2. Initialize sum = 0 for every starting index
3. Extend the subarray using another loop
4. Continuously add the current element to sum
5. Update maxSum with the maximum subarray sum found so far
6. Repeat for all possible starting indices
7. Return maxSum



class Solution {
    public int maxSubArray(int[] nums) {
        int maxSum = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        int sum = 0;
        for(int i=0; i<nums.length; i++){
            sum = 0;
            for(int j=i; j<nums.length; j++){
                sum += nums[j];
                maxSum = Math.max(maxSum, sum);
            }
        }
        return maxSum;
    }
}
